-- =====================================================================
-- MediSight DEMO SEED PACK  -  supabase/seed-demo.sql
-- =====================================================================
-- SYNTHETIC DEMONSTRATION DATA. Every person, hospital, phone number
-- and record in this file is fictional. Nothing here describes a real
-- patient, doctor or institution, and no real person's data was used.
--
-- PURPOSE: populate a LOCAL or STAGING Supabase project so the app can
-- be explored end to end (doctor directory, patient lists, risk queue,
-- risk trend, prediction reports, appointments, admin doctor approvals)
-- without any real data.
--
-- DO NOT run this on a production project. Before any real launch,
-- remove every demo row with the companion teardown script:
--   supabase/seed-demo-teardown.sql
--
-- HOW TO RUN: after all migrations are applied, run this file once in
-- the Supabase SQL Editor (or psql) as a privileged role. It is wrapped
-- in one transaction and is idempotent (ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING), so a
-- second run changes nothing.
--
-- IDENTIFIABILITY: every demo row carries a fixed UUID in the
-- d0000000-0000-4000-8000-xxxxxxxxxxxx namespace; every demo login uses
-- an @demo.medisight.local email; every clinical record uses an MRN of
-- the form DEMO-2026-NNNN. The teardown targets exactly these markers.
--
-- DEMO LOGINS (development only, never enable on a real project):
--   Doctors 1-12 : dr.<name>@demo.medisight.local   (see rows below)
--   Patients 1-8 : patient<n>@demo.medisight.local
--   Shared demo password for every demo account: Demo@12345
--   Doctor 12 is intentionally left in 'pending' status so the admin
--   doctor-approvals queue has something to review.
--
-- SOURCING (truthful provenance):
--   * Records structure and distributions follow two public synthetic
--     Kaggle datasets, downloaded on 2026-10-25 via Kaggle's public
--     download endpoint (no account data of any real person involved):
--       - "Multi-Location Healthcare Clinic Revenue Dataset" by
--         Nudrat Abbas (CC0: Public Domain) - multi-location clinic
--         structure; patient age/gender/chronic-condition distribution
--         (sampled below); appointment slots and fee spread.
--       - "Synthetic Hospital Visits and Billing Records" by
--         Aya A Saad (MIT) - department and diagnosis vocabulary and
--         the hospital-visit mix behind the demo histories.
--   * The datasets ship no identities (that is what makes them safe).
--     All names, hospitals, phone numbers and credentials in this pack
--     are fictional demo personas created for MediSight, localised to
--     Pakistan. Seeded predictions and explanations are illustrative
--     stored examples for the demo patients (severities follow the ML
--     service's own probability bands; confidence = max(p, 1 - p),
--     the service's definition) - they are not live model output.
--
-- NOTE: inserting 'Critical' demo predictions fires the database
-- trigger from 20260723143100_critical_alert_webhook.sql, which calls
-- the send-alert edge function via pg_net - on a local stack that is
-- the intended critical-alert pipeline exercising itself.
-- =====================================================================

BEGIN;

-- 1) Hospitals ------------------------------------------------------
ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

-- 2) Demo login accounts (auth.users; profiles are created by the
--    handle_new_user trigger from the metadata above) -----------------
ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

-- 3) Doctor directory details (profiles) ------------------------------
